== Polish Enhance (Refine Node 28) ==
[[File:Screenshot 2026-04-25 191027.png|thumb|Polishing Enhance tab]]
Polish Enhance is a mostly minor mechanic unlocked through Refine Node 28. There are five upgrades, one for each polish weapon, and each level increases the respective polish upgrade's efficiency by 1%.

However, the cost for each upgrade scales exponentially, so it is only viable in the late game.

== Runes (Node 35) ==
{{Stub|notes=table formula for price scaling and generation rate1 decrease}}
[[File:Screenshot 2026-04-25 191022.png|thumb|The Runes tab]]
Runes are a game mechanic vital to late-game progression. Runes are divided into 2 separate categories: Sun Runes and Moon Runes, each having 2 unique upgrades and 2 similar upgrades (see table below (TBA)). Moon generates faster than Sun but this is because Moon GRA upgrade (Generation Rate Amount, not to be confused with Generation Rate) is more expensive. Runes is a huge time wall between the refinement stage and the elements stage, often taking close to 2 weeks (from runes unlock to achievement 320) with minimal gameplay all throughout. They both generate at a rate of 1 every 10 days by default but are affected by local gamespeed and TF. Runes can be obtained faster by some nodes (eg. node 48), relic 34, upgrading their respective GRA (this costs runes) or by reducing the time it takes to generate Runes (by buying their respective first upgrades with RfP).
